---
source: crates/cli/tests/native.rs
expression: run.stdout
---
A pattern's matches in a text, with their groups and where they are

Usage: tw regex match [OPTIONS] [VALUE]

Arguments:
  [VALUE]  The input itself; stdin when left out, or -

Options:
  -e, --regexp <TEXT>  The regular expression
      --ignore-case    Match upper and lower case alike (i)
      --multi-line     ^ and $ match at the start and end of each line (m)
      --dot-all        . matches a newline too (s)
      --extended       White space in the pattern is ignored and # starts a comment (x)
      --pcre           Allow look-around and backreferences, by backtracking (fancy-regex)
      --first          Stop at the first match
  -i, --input <FILE>   Read the input from FILE
      --json           Write the result as JSON
      --no-newline     Do not end text output with a newline
  -h, --help           Print help
